  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Top government contractors list for FY2026 to date shows government contract obligations totaling $250B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. leads the ranking with $19.9B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP follows with $14.5B, and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO follows with $13.4B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice with $12.7B and $12.6B. MCKESSON CORPORATION has $12.3B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION has $11.3B, THE BOEING COMPANY appears twice with $9B and $6.1B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY has $8.6B. The list is a snapshot of fiscal-year-to-date obligations; current-year totals are partial. Contractors in this ranking are ordered by reported obligations for FY2026 to date, which gives a sense of which firms currently receive the largest shares of obligated federal contract dollars. Readers should treat the totals as interim figures for the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who leads the FY2026 to date contractor rankings?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. leads the FY2026 to date rankings with $19.9B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is second with $14.5B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is third with $13.4B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice in the top ranks with $12.7B and $12.6B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the total $250B represent?",
        "body": "The $250B figure is the total of contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The $250B total reflects partial-year obligations and not final fiscal-year totals."
      }
    ]
  },
